 "answer": "**Solution:**\n\nSince 151 is prime and gcd(75,151)=1, Fermat's Little Theorem gives 75^150 \u2261 1 (mod 151).\n\n616 = 4\u00b7150 + 16, so 75^616 \u2261 75^16 (mod 151).\n\nCompute powers by repeated squaring:\n\n- 75\u00b2 = 5625 \u2261 5625 \u2212 37\u00b7151 = 5625 \u2212 5587 = 38 (mod 151)\n- 75\u2074 \u2261 38\u00b2 = 1444 \u2261 1444 \u2212 9\u00b7151 = 1444 \u2212 1359 = 85 (mod 151)\n- 75\u2078 \u2261 85\u00b2 = 7225 \u2261 7225 \u2212 47\u00b7151 = 7225 \u2212 7097 = 128 (mod 151)\n- 75\u00b9\u2076 \u2261 128\u00b2 = 16384 \u2261 16384 \u2212 108\u00b7151 = 16384 \u2212 16308 = 76 (mod 151)\n\nSo 75^616 \u2261 76 (mod 151).\n\nFINAL: 76"
